1
00:00:05,444 --> 00:00:06,478
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:06,544 --> 00:00:09,084
Today, a tutorial
on the "backward stand-up wheel walk".

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,570
Let's go!

4
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:18,325
First, a demo
of the "backward stand-up wheel walk".

5
00:00:19,629 --> 00:00:23,695
In this trick, you stand
on the unicycle's wheel

6
00:00:23,872 --> 00:00:25,370
and move backward.

7
00:00:30,351 --> 00:00:33,538
When you start practicing,
hold on to a wall.

8
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:37,234
Put the foot that brakes the tire
on the frame,

9
00:00:37,365 --> 00:00:38,973
sticking out over the front of the tire.

10
00:00:39,263 --> 00:00:42,550
Your back foot
is the one that pushes the tire.

11
00:00:44,197 --> 00:00:47,933
Once you've got that,
stand up and squeeze the saddle firmly

12
00:00:47,992 --> 00:00:49,148
between your knees.

13
00:00:49,625 --> 00:00:53,934
Practice pushing the tire backward
with your back foot,

14
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:56,713
and braking it with your front foot,

15
00:00:56,817 --> 00:01:00,264
but releasing it as soon as
your back foot pushes the tire.

16
00:01:01,411 --> 00:01:03,945
Now try letting go of the wall.

17
00:01:04,191 --> 00:01:06,179
To get
into the "backward stand-up wheel walk",

18
00:01:06,344 --> 00:01:09,887
ride normally,
then brake to a stop.

19
00:01:09,911 --> 00:01:12,791
The first foot off the pedal
is your front foot,

20
00:01:12,863 --> 00:01:15,191
which goes on the frame
and the front of the tire,

21
00:01:15,549 --> 00:01:17,445
and then you take off your other foot,

22
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:20,745
the back one,
which starts pushing the tire.

23
00:01:21,237 --> 00:01:24,145
You can also combine it
with other tricks,

24
00:01:24,204 --> 00:01:27,951
like I do in the video,
and you'll find plenty more.

25
00:01:28,084 --> 00:01:31,371
To get out, go straight back
to the pedals.

26
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:35,551
The first foot back on the pedals
is your back foot.

27
00:01:36,677 --> 00:01:41,342
Or you can go into another trick,
like I do with a forward "wheel walk",

28
00:01:41,406 --> 00:01:45,430
where I sit back down on the saddle
and then get back on the pedals.

29
00:01:48,964 --> 00:01:53,110
Good luck, have a good session,
and I look forward to seeing your videos!

